@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false

autonumber
actor Shawn
participant "Gym Buddy" as App
participant "HealthConnectAdapter" as Adapter
participant "Android Health Connect" as HC
participant "RENPHO / Other Health Apps" as Source
participant "HealthAggregator" as Agg
participant "WorkoutRepository" as Repo
database "Room / SQLite" as DB

opt upstream health app syncs data
  Source -> HC : weight / body fat / sleep / HR / steps
end

Shawn -> App : open app / refresh context
App -> Adapter : refresh(date range)
Adapter -> HC : check permissions + availability

alt permissions granted
  Adapter -> HC : read SleepSessionRecord
  HC --> Adapter : sleep records
  Adapter -> HC : read WeightRecord / BodyFatRecord
  HC --> Adapter : body-composition records
  Adapter -> HC : read RestingHeartRate / Steps / ActiveCalories
  HC --> Adapter : health/activity records
  Adapter -> Adapter : normalize + deduplicate in memory
  Adapter -> Agg : normalized permitted records
  Agg -> Agg : build DailyHealthSummary
  Agg -> Agg : weekly median weight/body-fat + sample counts
  Agg -> Repo : upsert compact summaries only
  Repo -> DB : persist DailyHealthSummary / WeeklyBodyComposition
  Repo --> App : current compact context
  Agg -> Agg : discard fine-grained imported records after aggregation
else permissions unavailable or denied
  Adapter --> App : health integration unavailable
  App --> Shawn : workout monitoring still fully usable
end

note over App,DB
Health Connect is optional context and never in the camera-analysis critical path.
Missing, stale or denied health data must not block a workout.
end note

note over Adapter,Agg
Fine-grained Health Connect records are processing inputs,
not durable Gym Buddy records.
Keep long-term daily summaries and weekly body-composition snapshots only.
end note

note over Source,HC
RENPHO integration is indirect when possible.
Gym Buddy does not depend on a proprietary RENPHO API.
Upstream apps may have their own cloud behavior outside Gym Buddy's boundary.
end note

@enduml
